## Add Studio context-menu group assignment (exclusive membership)

Context: Users needed to assign selected Studio entities to an existing
ontology group from the right-click menu (including multi-select), and to
see clearly that an entity can belong to only one group across modal,
General tab, and menus. Backend exclusive membership was already enforced.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   Add assignEntitiesToStudioGroup + Add to group flyout on single and
   multi-select context menus (with Remove from group when applicable).
2. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   Context-menu submenu styles; overflow visible for flyouts.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-groups.js
   Confirm when selecting a member already in another group.
4. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_groups.html
   Exclusive-membership copy in the group modal.
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   General-tab hint: one group per entity.
6. docs/user-guide.md
   Document right-click Add to group and exclusive membership.
7. tests/units/front/test_map_context_menu_tabs.py
   Contract for Add to group wiring.
8. tests/units/front/test_ontology_map_multi_select.py
   Multi-select menu wires group membership.
9. tests/units/front/test_studio_views_groups_contract.py
   Exclusive-membership UI surface contract.

