## Rename Business Views from the Studio View dropdown

Context: The Studio View filter was a plain select with no way to rename a
Business View, although POST /domain/design-views/rename already existed and
was tested. The dropdown now follows the Groups menu pattern: each view row has
a pick item and a pencil that opens a rename modal.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_map.html
   Replace the #studioViewSelect <select> with a btn-group dropdown
   (#studioViewBtn, #studioViewMenu) keeping All, view rows, and the delete button.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   refreshStudioViewSelect rebuilds the rich menu; new renameStudioView modal
   calls /domain/design-views/rename with a client-side duplicate check;
   wireStudioViewControls handles pick and pencil clicks.
3. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   Replace .studio-view-select with toggle, menu, check-mark and row styles.
4. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   Hide .studio-view-rename for viewer and read-only roles.
5. docs/user-guide.md
   Document renaming a Business View from the View dropdown.
6. tests/units/front/test_studio_views_groups_contract.py
   Update ids to the new dropdown; add rename wiring contract.
7. tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py
   studioViewSelect rendering check now targets studioViewBtn.
8. tests/units/front/test_help_center_menu_sync.py
   Same id update.

